# Ignite Core

Canonical sources (read them; do not duplicate them here):
- Product/business/architecture: [`docs/product/PRD.md`](docs/product/PRD.md)
- How we build: [`docs/development/Ignite_Development_Playbook.md`](docs/development/Ignite_Development_Playbook.md)
- Folder layout: [`ARCHITECTURE.md`](ARCHITECTURE.md)

## Truth and scope

- The canonical PRD is the product/business/architecture source of truth.
- Explicit current product-owner decisions override older implementation assumptions (playbook §1).
- Before significant product or business-rule work, read the relevant PRD sections.
- Do not implement features the PRD explicitly defers (PRD §§54–55).
- Do not silently invent unresolved business rules; ask or record the gap.
- Keep work scoped to the requested sprint/phase. Avoid broad refactors unless required.

## Architecture

- Preserve dependency direction: Presentation → Feature/Application → Domain → Repository → Persistence (PRD §§27–28, 39).
- UI must not call Firebase/Firestore directly.
- Firebase is infrastructure, not the Ignite domain model. Domain types stay independent of Firestore documents and Firebase APIs.

## Domain invariants

- Respect strict Season isolation: seasons do not share curriculum or learning state (PRD §§5, 7).
- Respect active-season content immutability once a season is Active/Locked (PRD §6).
- Learning state is owned by Quizzer + Season + MaterialSet + Card, not by Deck (PRD §§13.4, 15).

## Configuration vs literals

- Do not hard-code season, division, tournament, entitlement, mastery, product, environment, or similar business values when they belong in configuration or domain policy (playbook §6).
- Named local layout/animation constants are allowed. Values that encode product behavior are not.
